y_completion again — that wastes turns and burns your budget. End the task with the answer.\n\nMEMORY HAS THESE FACTS — copy these exact strings into your finalAnswer:\n  - source_1_title: \"Renewable energy - Wikipedia\"\n  - source_1_summary: \"Renewable energy (also called green energy) is energy made from renewable natural resources that are replenished on a human timescale. The most widely used renewable energy types are solar energy, wind power, and hydropower. Bioenergy and geothermal power are also significant in some countries. Renewable energy installations can be large or small and are suited for both urban and rural areas.\"\n  - source_2_title: \"Wind power - Wikipedia\"\n  - source_2_summary: \"Wind power is the use of wind energy to generate useful work. Historically, wind power was used by sails, windmills and windpumps, but today it is mostly used to generate electricity. This article deals only with wind power for electricity generation. Today, wind power is generated almost completely using wind turbines, generally grouped into wind farms and connected to the electrical grid.\"\n  - source_3_title: \"Solar power - Wikipedia\"\n  - source_3_summary: \"Solar power, also known as solar electricity, is the conversion of energy from sunlight into electricity, either directly using photovoltaics (PV) or indirectly using concentrated solar power. Solar panels use the photovoltaic effect to convert light into an electric current.\"\n\nRequired shape: 'Based on page[0] and page[1]..., the answer is: <values from memory above>. Source: <URL>.'\n=== END STAGNATION SIGNAL ===\n\n=== WORKING MEMORY (carried across turns) ===\n  - source_1_title = \"Renewable energy - Wikipedia\"  (evidence: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Renewable_energy page heading)\n  - source_1_summary = \"Renewable energy (also called green energy) is energy made from renewable natural resources that are replenished on a hu\"  (evidence: First paragraph of https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ren